      "content": "exactly. it's like i'm just watching my life happen in low resolution. everyone else seems to be living in color, but i'm just stuck in this gray, lukewarm existence where nothing matters. if the ceiling is already reached and it's this low, isn't it just more honest to admit that the whole pursuit was a mistake? like, why keep pretending there's some deeper meaning in just being a background character?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
